      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Verso",
          "value": "<ol>\n<li>Then there transpired that which a book</li>\n<li>would prove insufficient to describe. Next, caskets were brought</li>\n<li>and he began to eat lemon cakes.</li>\n<li>We stayed [just] for a while but he detained me</li>\n<li>in order that we confer a moment confidentially.</li>\n<li>The master seemed favourably inclined. In the meantime</li>\n<li>Rabbi Avraham, may God protect him, had taught al-Jal\u0101l</li>\n<li>a term with which to address</li>\n<li>Rabbi Moshe. Upon his reciting it [Rabbi Moshe] laughed</li>\n<li>with amusement and sported with the [child].</li>\n<li>I was the first to leave [the house],</li>\n<li>while al-Jal\u0101l remained behind talking to the usher</li>\n<li>in the vestibule. Whereupon Rabbi Moshe</li>\n<li>enquired of Rabbi Avraham, \"Where has his son gone?\"</li>\n<li>\"He is standing by the door,\" he replied.</li>\n<li>\"Go and call him,\" he said, while re-entering [the door],</li>\n<li>whereupon he came across the [child who again] recited the form of address.</li>\n<li>Peace.</li>\n</ol>",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
